    "['no shutdown', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'delete shutdown', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\ndelete shutdown\\n##\\n\\nExplanation: \\n- In Cisco, `no shutdown` enables an interface (brings it up administratively). \\n- The Juniper equivalent is `delete shutdown`, which removes any shutdown configuration on the interface, effectively enabling it. \\n- Juniper interfaces are up by default, but this command is used if the interface was previously manually shut down.', 'trans_template': 'delete shutdown'}]]": 1,
